# SP0 step 1: the repository skeleton. No cloud account is involved: these are
# files in the repo.
# Format: file | regular expression the file must contain | message if it doesn't
terraform/backend.tf | ^  required_version = ">= 1\.10"$ | the version pin must be >= 1.10, the release that made native S3 locking possible
.gitignore | ^\.terraform/$ | provider binaries and module cache are never committed
.gitignore | ^\*\.tfstate$ | state never goes into git
.gitignore | ^\*\.tfstate\.\*$ | nor do the temporary files OpenTofu writes beside it
.gitignore | ^\*\.tfvars$ | local values, possibly secrets
.gitignore | ^!\*\.tfvars\.example$ | the example file is committed, so a reader knows what to set
.gitignore | ^node_modules/$ | installed, not authored
.gitignore | ^dist/$ | compiled output, rebuilt by CI
.gitignore | ^build/$ | the same
.gitignore | ^scratch/$ | local files the money milestones create
.gitignore | ^secrets/$ | the Postgres password file in SP10
README.md | ^# serverless-pipeline$ | the repo title is the first heading
